   "text": "This SMILES was read directly from the drawing, so the points below are my own reading of it.\n\n**Ring and chain assembly**\n- **Macrocycle ester:** a piperazic acid ring whose carboxyl is esterified to an O\u2013CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013CH2 linker. That linker attaches to C3 of the indole.\n- **Indole:** N-ethyl, with a 2-(1-methoxyethyl)pyridin-3-yl group at C2. C5 is bonded to a 3-hydroxyphenyl ring.\n- **Phenyl side chain:** the phenyl ring carries CH2\u2013CH(NH\u2013)\u2013C(=O) at the 5-position, and that carbonyl acylates the piperazic ring nitrogen.\n- **Amide chain on the NH:** the NH is acylated by an N-methyl valine unit. Its N-methyl nitrogen carries a pyrrolidine-3-carbonyl group.\n- **Warhead:** the pyrrolidine nitrogen is acylated by C(=O)\u2013C\u2261C\u2013(N-methylpyrrolidin-2-yl).\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI assigned each wedged or hashed centre from the drawing, working out the CIP descriptor first and then the matching @/@@:\n- Piperazic \u03b1-carbon (hashed bond to the carbonyl): S\n- Phenylalanine-derived \u03b1-carbon (wedged NH): S\n- Valine \u03b1-carbon (wedged isopropyl): S\n- Pyrrolidine-3 carbon (wedged carbonyl): S\n- N-methylpyrrolidin-2 carbon (wedged alkyne): S\n- Methoxyethyl carbon (wedged methyl): S\n\nThe drawing also shows a wedge at the pyridine/indole biaryl bond, which looks like an atropisomer marker. I left it out because it cannot be written as a simple tetrahedral stereocentre in SMILES.\n\nSMILES: O=C1OCC(C)(C)Cc2c(-c3cccnc3[C@H](C)OC)n(CC)c3ccc(cc23)-c2cc(O)cc(c2)C[C@H](NC(=O)[C@H](C(C)C)N(C)C(=O)[C@H]2CCN(C2)C(=O)C#C[C@@H]2CCCN2C)C(=O)N2CCC[C@@H]1N2"
